{
  "_README": [
    "Profanity substitution tables for the TTS profanity filter (off by default).",
    "Authored by hand, not generated at runtime: languageBoost has a closed set of",
    "values, so there is nothing to discover at request time.",
    "",
    "Rules enforced by tests/unit/profanityLists.test.js:",
    "  - terms are lowercase, unique within a language, and non-empty",
    "  - replacements are non-empty (an empty one lets a message reduce to \"\",",
    "    which every caller drops silently instead of speaking)",
    "  - no term equals its own replacement",
    "  - no replacement collides with another term in the same language",
    "",
    "confidence records how well covered a language is. Where coverage is thin the",
    "list is a short high-confidence core rather than a padded guess: a missing",
    "entry degrades to unfiltered text, which is no worse than the feature being",
    "off, whereas a wrong substitution is actively bad. Languages marked 'low'",
    "want review by a native speaker."
  ],
